  "name": "ANTI MOG (MYELIN OLIGODENDROCYTE GLYCOPROTEIN) SERUM",
  "code": "1993",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Note :</strong><br>Auto Immune reactivity are not by themselves diagnostic and must be correlated with other laboratory and clinical findings.Test conducted on 1:10 diluted serum.<br>Antigen substrate - transfected cells of EU-90.</p>\n<p><strong>Comments:</strong><br>NMO (Neuromyelitis optica) is a chronic autoimmune disease of CNS with different manifestations (NMO spectrum disease;NMOSD). Antibodies against water channel aquaporin-4 which is expressed on astrocytes, are established biomarkers for&nbsp;NMOSD and are detectable in 60% to 90% of patients. In 7.4% of cases, however, antibodies against MOG are also&nbsp;produced. In NMOSD patient who are anti-aquaporin-4 negative, MOG antibodies occur in 21.1% of sera. Determination of&nbsp;autoantibodies against MOG is especially relevant for the diagnosis of acquired demyelinating diseases of the CNS,&nbsp;particularly in children, and NMO in adults. 30%-40% of patients with inflammatory demyelinating disease of the CNS show<br>antibodies against MOG at disease onset.</p>",
